{
  "source": "course-assets/people-skills/people-skills.mp4",
  "duration": 127.68,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.56,
      "text": "Your group just finished the semester's history project."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.3,
      "end": 6.88,
      "text": "Most of your group feels great because the big project is finally complete."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.76,
      "end": 10.6,
      "text": "But Maya notices a problem and starts suggesting a change."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.46,
      "end": 11.94,
      "text": "Someone interrupts."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.88,
      "end": 13.36,
      "text": "We are done."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.94,
      "end": 14.34,
      "text": "No more suggestions."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.46,
      "end": 17.22,
      "text": "Maya goes quiet and the group moves on."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.34,
      "end": 21.0,
      "text": "You notice that Maya's expression and body language changed."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.18,
      "end": 23.42,
      "text": "What would you say or do next?"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.26,
      "end": 26.0,
      "text": "This is a moment to use your people skills."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.8,
      "end": 28.26,
      "text": "This board lays out your next move."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.8,
      "end": 31.82,
      "text": "Ask, Maya, we didn't hear the rest of your idea."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.26,
      "end": 32.76,
      "text": "Do you want to finish?"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.58,
      "end": 35.08,
      "text": "Show her that what she says matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.84,
      "end": 36.7,
      "text": "Maya has a point."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.24,
      "end": 40.2,
      "text": "The third example misses the instructions, helping the group improve."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.78,
      "end": 44.36,
      "text": "Even if the group had ultimately decided to keep the draft exactly as it was,"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.8,
      "end": 47.2,
      "text": "her idea deserved to be heard and considered."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.16,
      "end": 50.56,
      "text": "This graphic shows four ways to strengthen your people skills."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.14,
      "end": 52.14,
      "text": "You can practice them every day."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.92,
      "end": 54.8,
      "text": "The first practice is to listen to understand."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.8,
      "end": 58.06,
      "text": "Do not plan your reply while the other person is talking."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.7,
      "end": 62.18,
      "text": "Instead, ask one genuine follow-up question before offering your opinion."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.16,
      "end": 65.64,
      "text": "The second practice is to notice what isn't being said."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.36,
      "end": 70.44,
      "text": "Pay attention to tone, hesitation, enthusiasm and changes in behavior."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.38,
      "end": 74.16,
      "text": "If you're unsure what a change in someone's behavior means, ask."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.0,
      "end": 77.0,
      "text": "The third practice is to show people they matter."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.76,
      "end": 80.8,
      "text": "Remember what they tell you and give specific appreciation for their work."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.42,
      "end": 83.7,
      "text": "Make sure to give people credit when an idea is theirs."
    },
    {
      "start": 83.7,
      "end": 87.44,
      "text": "The fourth practice is to challenge ideas, not people."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.12,
      "end": 90.22,
      "text": "Address difficult things directly and calmly."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.06,
      "end": 94.3,
      "text": "You must challenge the idea or behavior without attacking the person."
    },
    {
      "start": 95.18,
      "end": 97.36,
      "text": "People skills matter even more in the AI future."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.46,
      "end": 99.3,
      "text": "First, you'll stand out."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.0,
      "end": 103.2,
      "text": "As AI normalizes polished work, collaboration sets you apart."
    },
    {
      "start": 104.38,
      "end": 105.7,
      "text": "Second, trust still matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.42,
      "end": 108.58,
      "text": "People choose teammates who listen and keep promises."
    },
    {
      "start": 109.86,
      "end": 110.9,
      "text": "Third, connection matters."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.9,
      "end": 114.0,
      "text": "AI helps with work, but people need to feel valued."
    },
    {
      "start": 114.92,
      "end": 115.86,
      "text": "AI can write it."
    },
    {
      "start": 116.28,
      "end": 117.94,
      "text": "It can't be the person in the room."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.7,
      "end": 122.88,
      "text": "Listen well, speak clearly and be someone people want to work with."
    }
  ],
